      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Atchinson & Nebraska Railroad built its line to Lincoln in 1871, it cut through Roca, leading to a siding and station that needed a name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
